# Git identity and naming

Mandatory. Present and future.

## Identity

Every commit must be authored and committed only by:

- Name: `David Ramirez`
- Email: `rxgdavid@gmail.com`

Set `user.name` and `user.email` to those values before committing. Pass the same identity as `GIT_AUTHOR_*` and `GIT_COMMITTER_*` if the environment defaults to something else.

## Forbidden references

Nothing in git metadata or naming may refer to Cursor, bots, or agent tooling:

| Surface | Forbidden |
|---|---|
| Author name / email | `Cursor`, `Cursor Agent`, `cursoragent@…`, any `*bot*` |
| Committer name / email | Same as author |
| Commit message body or subject | Words or trailers that cite Cursor, bot, agent, or AI tooling as author |
| `Co-authored-by` / other trailers | `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, bot accounts, or agent identities |
| Branch names | `cursor/…`, `*bot*`, `*agent*` as product/author branding in the name |

## Never

- Author or committer `Cursor`, `Cursor Agent`, or `cursoragent@cursor.com`
- `Co-authored-by: Cursor` (or any Cursor / bot co-author)
- A Cursor author with the user as co-author (or the reverse)
- Commit messages that credit Cursor, a bot, or an agent
- Branch names that advertise Cursor or a bot

If a hook or wrapper injects a Cursor trailer or wrong author, strip it before the commit is created (or amend immediately so HEAD has no Cursor / bot attribution).
